  "description": "Owner ruling 2026-09-12 ('resolve functionals ... what lean provable'): prop:unified-iterative-correction and hecke_core_legacy.unified_iterative_correction are different functionals, and the block's displayed formula CANNOT denote the producer's. The summand ln|tr M| - ln d is even in the trace, so the block's total is invariant under flipping any block trace's sign; the producer's Pass-2 gate keeps exactly tr <= 0 and therefore reads a datum the summand has destroyed. Measured here: both totals reproduced in mpf from the final traces alone; ungated/gated = 4.60 (2H) and 3.40 (4He); the sign flip leaves the ungated total identical and moves the gated one; no active block sits at tr = 0, so genuine complementary slackness (tight means tr = 0, not tr <= 0) selects the empty set; deleting the q-Laplacian resolvent the block omits moves the gated total by >2x; and y_lambda matches neither reading of 'LP shadow price'. Lean: QOU.MassTheory.UICFunctionalSelection (sorry-free).",
